desc:RapReaper Ducks (volume dips drawn by RapReaper)
//author:RapReaper
//tags:utility gain
// RapReaper's duck_section draws dips in this plug-in's one control as a parameter envelope. The control runs
// from 0 to 1 on purpose: REAPER applies an FX parameter envelope in the control's own units, and the bridge
// RapReaper talks through only ever writes envelope values between 0 and 1. (A dB slider, such as the stock
// Volume/Pan Smoother's, would read those values as dB, so a dip drawn as 0.83 would become +0.83 dB.)
// 1 = full level (0 dB), 0 = -40 dB; in between, the dB go down in a straight line. A few milliseconds of
// smoothing take the steps out of block-rate automation; the envelope's own fades do the rest.

slider1:1<0,1,0.0001>Level (0 = -40 dB, 1 = full)

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

@init
MAX_DIP_DB = 40;
g = 1;                                   // the gain applied right now
target = 1;
coef = 1 - exp(-1 / (0.002 * srate));    // about 2 ms toward the target

@slider
level = min(max(slider1, 0), 1);
target = 10 ^ (-MAX_DIP_DB * (1 - level) / 20);

@sample
g += (target - g) * coef;
spl0 *= g;
spl1 *= g;
